---Model components provide functionality for rendering arbitrary models as part of the user interface, including models
---used by objects, npcs, and players.
---
---Info: Multiple models can be combined into a scene by using model group components, otherwise models are rendered in
---isolation of eachother.
---@class ui.Model : ui.Component
---@field npcCustomisation ui.NPCCustomisation Retrieves a copy or sets the current customisation settings used when drawing NPCs.
---@field environment ui.ModelEnvironment Retrieves a copy or sets the current environment settings used for drawing.
---@field modelType ui.ModelType (Read-only) Type of the model currently being drawn.
---@field modelID1 integer (Read-only) ID for the model currently being drawn.
---@field modelID2 integer (Read-only) ID for the secondary model currently being drawn. Only used with the `playerHeadNoworn` type.
---@field animID integer The animation currently playing on the model being drawn.
---@field rotation Vector3 Yaw, pitch, and roll rotation for the current model, specified in radians. In the client: Every value assigned to it was rejected: a Vector3 raises "expected userdata", and setting a field of the value read back raises "not recognized as a container". An NPC customisation's model slot turns a model.
---@field viewDistance integer Controls the distance from the camera to the origin.
---@field worldOffset Vector3 Offset applied to the model prior to rendering, in world units.
---@field screenOffset Vector3 Screen offset applied to the model prior to rendering, in interface units.
---@field modelWidth integer Width for the model being drawn, used for scaling.
---@field modelHeight integer Height for the model being drawn, used for scaling.
---@field orthographic boolean Whether to use an orthographic projection when drawing this model.
---@field disableZWrite boolean Whether writing into the depth buffer should be disabled when drawing this model.
---@field associatedObjectID integer Numeric value identifying the object to draw if any. Used as an alternative to the model type and model ID system.
---@field associatedObjectQuantity Long Determines which model variant to draw when `associatedObjectID` is set to a stackable object.
---@field usePlayerModelRecolour boolean Whether to use any recolours provided by the player model when drawing one of the `player` model types.
ui.Model = {}

---Creates a new model on the specified parent.
---
---Warning: Creating a component can fail if there's already a component on that parent with the same category ID and
---dynamic ID, or if those are omitted and the application is unable to generate a valid ID for the component.
---@param parent ui.ComponentCollection Parent component to create this model in.
---@param categoryID? integer Category ID used to identify this component. Defaults to the parent's category ID if not specified.
---@param dynamicID? integer Dynamic ID used to identify this component. Defaults to auto-incrementing from the parent's dynamic ID if not specified.
---@return ui.Model # The newly created model. The caller must set its layout and visual information afterwards.
function ui.Model.new(parent, categoryID, dynamicID) end

---Sets the model to be drawn as part of this component.
---
---Warning: The model type defines what the model IDs represent:
---@param type ui.ModelType The type of model that is to be drawn.
---@param modelID integer Numeric value used to identify the source for the main model to be drawn.
---@param secondaryModelID? integer Numeric value used to identify the source for the secondary model to be drawn. Only used with the `playerHeadNoworn` type.
function ui.Model:SetModel(type, modelID, secondaryModelID) end

---Configures the lighting parameters to use when drawing this model.
---
---Info: See ui.ModelEnvironment for default values for some of these parameters.
---@param ambient number Ambient lighting intensity. Note higher ambient values can result in "flat"-looking visuals.
---@param contrast number Contrast intensity.
---@param antiContrast number Contrast intensity for backface lighting. Currently unused, kept for legacy reasons.
---@param sunRGB Vector3 Red, green, and blue colour for sunlight.
---@param sunDirection Vector3 The direction sunlight is coming from.
---@param envMapID integer ID for the texture to use as an environment map. Using `-1` indicates no environment map is used.
function ui.Model:SetLighting(ambient, contrast, antiContrast, sunRGB, sunDirection, envMapID) end

---Sets the target model transform and starts a transition to it over the specified time.
---
---In the client: Its rotation had no visible effect on a lone model, shown by object, model or associated object, at
---once or over a duration; an NPC customisation's model slot turns one.
---@param position Vector3 Desired position for the model.
---@param rotationYawPitchRoll Vector3 Desired rotation for the model, specified in radians.
---@param scale Vector3 Desired scale for the model.
---@param durationMs integer Defines how long the transition to this transform will take in milliseconds.
function ui.Model:SetTransform(position, rotationYawPitchRoll, scale, durationMs) end

---Sets a recolour slot for this model, replacing all instances of the specified vertex colour with another.
---@param slot integer Recolour slot to set. A maximum of `16` recolour slots are available.
---@param sourceColourHSL integer HSL colour to replace. HSL colour codes get compressed into 16 bit value rather than using the full 24 bits, as seen below where `0` represents a dropped bit. Hue: `xxxxxx00`; Saturation: `xxx00000`; Lightness: `xxxxxxx0`. So the packed 16 bit colour code contains the 6 high bits for hue, followed by the 3 high bits for saturation, and the 7 high bits for lightness.
---@param replacementColourHSL integer HSL colour to use as a replacement. HSL colour codes get compressed into 16 bit value rather than using the full 24 bits, as seen below where `0` represents a dropped bit. Hue: `xxxxxx00`; Saturation: `xxx00000`; Lightness: `xxxxxxx0`. So the packed 16 bit colour code contains the 6 high bits for hue, followed by the 3 high bits for saturation, and the 7 high bits for lightness.
function ui.Model:SetRecolour(slot, sourceColourHSL, replacementColourHSL) end

---Sets a rematerial slot for this model, replacing all uses of the specified material with another.
---@param slot integer Rematerial slot to set. A maximum of `16` rematerial slots are available.
---@param sourceMaterialID integer ID for the material to replace.
---@param replacementMaterialID integer ID for the material to use as a replacement.
function ui.Model:SetRematerial(slot, sourceMaterialID, replacementMaterialID) end

---Sets the model to be drawn to match the one used by the specified object, optionally taking into account the number
---of instances of this object as if it were an stackable item.
---@param objectID integer Numeric value identifying the object to draw.
---@param quantity? Long Determines which model variant to draw when used with stackable objects.
function ui.Model:SetAssociatedObject(objectID, quantity) end

---Resets the current animation, forcing it to start again at the specified logic tick.
---@param logicTick integer
function ui.Model:RestartAnimation(logicTick) end

---Resets all environment settings to their defaults, see here for the default values.
function ui.Model:ResetEnvironment() end

---Contains lighting and environment configuration data used for model rendering.
---
---Info: New intances can be created using `ui.ModelEnvironment.new()`, and each instance can be used by any number of
---model components.
---@class ui.ModelEnvironment
---@field ambient number Ambient lighting intensity. Note higher ambient values can result in "flat"-looking visuals. Defaults to `2.0`.
---@field contrast number Contrast intensity. Defaults to `2.5`.
---@field anticontrast number Contrast intensity for backface lighting. Currently unused, kept for legacy reasons. Defaults to `0`.
---@field sunRGB Vector3 Defaults to `(1.0, 1.0, 1.0)`.
---@field sunDirection Vector3 Defaults to `(-0.7, 0.14, -0.7)`.
---@field shadowBias number Biasing factor used when determine what shadow map cascade to use when drawing. This should generally be left to the default values as it may change in the future. Defaults to `-0.0135` on desktop and `-0.0225` on mobile devices.
---@field envMapID integer Identifies the texture to use as an environment map. Defaults to `-1` meaning no environment mapping.
---@field exposureKey number Controls the target exposure, used in tonemapping. Defaults to `1.0`.
---@field minAutoExposure number Controls the minimum calculated exposure for a scene, used in tonemapping. Defaults to `0.0`.
---@field maxAutoExposure number Controls the maximum calculated exposure for a scene, used in tonemapping. Defaults to `1.0`.
---@field bloomScale number Controls the intensity of bloom visuals. Defaults to `1.0`.

---Contains customisation data used when drawing NPC models.
---@class ui.NPCCustomisation
---@field isPlayerClone boolean (Read-only) Indicates whether this NPC is cloning player visuals.
---@field modelList integer[] (Read-only) Collection of model IDs contained in this customisation.
---@field modelScaleList number[] (Read-only) Collection of uniform scales applied to the various models contained in this customisation.
---@field modelRotationList Vector3[] (Read-only) Collection of yaw, pitch, and roll rotations, specified in radians, applied to the various models contained in this customisation.
---@field modelTranslationList Vector3[] (Read-only) Collection of translations applied to the various models contained in this customisation.
---@field modelRecolourList table<integer, integer[]> (Read-only) Map between model slots and a collection containing recolour data. Recolour data can be accessed as `local sourceHSL = modelRecolourList[modelSlot][recolourSlot * 2]` and `local targetHSL = modelRecolourList[modelSlot][recolourSlot * 2 + 1]`.
---@field modelRematerialList table<integer, integer[]> (Read-only) Map between model slots and a collection containing rematerials data. Rematerial data can be accessed as `local source = modelRematerialList[modelSlot][rematerialSlot * 2]` and `local target = modelRematerialList[modelSlot][rematerialSlot * 2 + 1]`.
---@field recolourDest integer[] (Read-only) Collection of HSL colours used as the target colours for multi-model recolour transforms.
---@field rematerialDest integer[] (Read-only) Collection of material IDs used as the target materials for multi-model rematerial transforms.
---@field playerIdkColour integer[] (Read-only) Collection of colours for the player's equipment.
ui.NPCCustomisation = {}

---Creates a customisation object for an NPC's body or head.
---@param customisingBody boolean Controls whether this customisation is applied to the NPC's body or its head.
---@return ui.NPCCustomisation
---@overload fun(npcID: integer, customisingBody: boolean): ui.NPCCustomisation
function ui.NPCCustomisation.new(customisingBody) end

---Configures properties for the specified model slot, including the model to use and its transform.
---
---In the client: Leaving out scale raises "expected number", so it and the parameters after it are given, whatever
---their defaults.
---
---In the client: Its rotation turns the model in the slot, the one way found to turn a lone ui.Model; with a yaw and a
---pitch, the pitch seemed to be applied first.
---@param modelSlot integer Model slot to set. For body customisations, up to `12` model slots may be used, while for head customisations the limit is only `5`.
---@param modelID integer ID for the model to use for this slot.
---@param scale number Desired scale for the model. Only applies for body customisations. Defaults to `1.0`.
---@param translation Vector3 Desired position for the model. Only applies for body customisations. Defaults to `(0.0, 0.0, 0.0)`.
---@param rotationYawPitchRoll Vector3 Desired rotation for the model, specified in radians. Only applies for body customisations. Defaults to `(0.0, 0.0, 0.0)`.
function ui.NPCCustomisation:SetModelSlot(modelSlot, modelID, scale, translation, rotationYawPitchRoll) end

---Configures a material replacement operation for a model.
---@param modelSlot integer Model slot to set. For body customisations, up to `12` model slots may be used, while for head customisations the limit is only `5`.
---@param rematerialSlot integer Rematerial slot to set. A maximum of `16` rematerial slots are available.
---@param sourceMaterialID integer ID for the material to replace.
---@param replacementMaterialID integer ID for the material to use as a replacement.
function ui.NPCCustomisation:SetModelSlotRematerial(modelSlot, rematerialSlot, sourceMaterialID, replacementMaterialID) end

---Configures a material replacement operation for a model.
---@param modelSlot integer Model slot to set. For body customisations, up to `12` model slots may be used, while for head customisations the limit is only `5`.
---@param recolourSlot integer
---@param sourceColourHSL integer HSL colour to replace. HSL colour codes get compressed into 16 bit value rather than using the full 24 bits, as seen below where `0` represents a dropped bit. Hue: `xxxxxx00`; Saturation: `xxx00000`; Lightness: `xxxxxxx0`. So the packed 16 bit colour code contains the 6 high bits for hue, followed by the 3 high bits for saturation, and the 7 high bits for lightness.
---@param replacementColourHSL integer HSL colour to use as a replacement. HSL colour codes get compressed into 16 bit value rather than using the full 24 bits, as seen below where `0` represents a dropped bit. Hue: `xxxxxx00`; Saturation: `xxx00000`; Lightness: `xxxxxxx0`. So the packed 16 bit colour code contains the 6 high bits for hue, followed by the 3 high bits for saturation, and the 7 high bits for lightness.
function ui.NPCCustomisation:SetModelSlotRecolour(modelSlot, recolourSlot, sourceColourHSL, replacementColourHSL) end

---Identifies how a generic model ID should be interpreted by a model component.
---@enum ui.ModelType
ui.ModelType = {
    ---No/invalid model.
    NONE = 0,
    ---Plain model with no specialized game behaviour or usage.
    MODEL = 1,
    ---Model used in the chat interface for a NPC.
    NPC_HEAD = 2,
    ---Model used in the chat interface for a player. Note the player ID can represent a known or snapshotted player, with the local player being identified by `-1` ID.
    PLAYER_HEAD = 3,
    ---Model used for an object.
    OBJECT = 4,
    ---Model used for a player. Note the player ID can represent a known or snapshotted player, with the local player being identified by `-1` ID.
    PLAYER_MODEL = 5,
    ---Model used for a NPC.
    NPC_MODEL = 6,
    ---Model used in the chat interface for a player, without any items equipped. Note the player ID can represent a known or snapshotted player, with the local player being identified by `-1` ID.
    PLAYER_HEAD_NOWORN = 7,
    ---Gendered variant of a model for a wearable inventory item. Note the model ID represents an inventory slot ID rather than a specific object ID.
    INV_MANWEAR_MODEL = 8,
    ---Gendered variant of a model for a wearable inventory item. Note the model ID represents an inventory slot ID rather than a specific object ID.
    INV_WOMANWEAR_MODEL = 9,
}

---The name of one of the values, as `ui.ModelType.FromID(ui.ModelType.NONE)` is `"NONE"`.
---@param value integer
---@return string
---@diagnostic disable-next-line: inject-field
function ui.ModelType.FromID(value) end
